                <pb facs="0533" n="425" sameAs="frus:frus1893/pg425"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Señor Diaz to Señor Cayetano Romero.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Laredo, Tex.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-12-13"><hi rendition="#italic">December 13,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>The leader of the San Ignacio raid is called Maximo Martinez. Two bands, led by
                    one-eyed Francisco and Mangas de Agua, passed opposite Carrizo, saying that they
                    were going to cross over into Mexico between Mier and Gurrero. No action taken
                    here. They are awaiting orders at Fort McIntosh.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">L. Lameda Diaz.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
